trowd\cellx4400\cellx4600\cellx9400\intbl \cell\intbl )\cell\intbl DATED: {\field\flddirty{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\insrsid8152461  DATE \\@ "MMMM d, yyyy" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs22\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\insrsid8152461 February 7, 2014}}}\cell\row\trowd\cellx4400\cellx4600\cellx9400\intbl                      Agency.\cell\intbl )\cell\intbl \cell\row\trowd\cellx4400\cellx4600\cellx9400\intbl ___________________________________\cell\intbl )\cell\intbl \cell\row} {\pard\cf1\sl480\tabThe United States Postal Service (\'93Agency\'94 or \'93Postal Service\'94) responds to complainant %COMP_FN% %COMP_LN%\'27s written discovery requests as follows.   \par}\line{\pard\cf1\b\ul\qc I. Preliminary Statement\ul0\b\par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabThe Agency makes the following responses/objections to Complainant\'27s written discovery requests.  The responses and objections to the requests are made solely for the purpose of this action.  The Agency responds to Complainant\'27s requests based upon information available at this time and without prejudice to the production of subsequently discovered information or documents omitted despite having conducted a good faith search.  Further, the Agency does not waive its right to introduce such subsequently discovered information or documents into evidence.\par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabEach response and/or production of any documents described herein is subject to objections at trial or hearing, including those relating to competence, relevance, materiality, propriety, and admissibility.  The Agency is not making any incidental or implied admissions regarding the contents or admissibility of these documents by virtue of the production.  \par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabComplainant, by accepting receipt of the information and documents provided in response to Complainant\'27s First Set of Interrogatories, First Set of Requests for Production of Documents, and Request for Admissions, hereby implicitly agrees to keep said information and documents confidential and limit their use strictly to the proceedings in this action.  In the event Complainant does not agree to this confidentiality provision, Complainant is hereby requested to state all objections in writing within 10 days of receipt of this notice, so that the Agency can file a request for protective order as it deems appropriate.  \par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabInformation obtained in ongoing and future discovery, as well as conclusions resulting from continuing evaluation and analysis of information already in the Agency\'27s possession, is expected to add to the Agency\'27s knowledge and contentions with respect to matters set forth herein.  Therefore, the following responses are given without prejudice to the Agency\'27s right to produce evidence of any subsequently discovered fact or facts.\par}\line{\pard\cf1\ul\b\qc II. General Objections\b\ul0\par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabThe following responses are based upon information currently available to the Agency, and, except for explicit facts admitted herein, no incidental or implied admissions are intended hereby.  The fact that the Agency has responded or objected to any request or part thereof should not be taken as an admission that the Agency accepts or admits the existence of any facts set forth or assumed in such request, or that such response constitutes admissible evidence.  The fact that the Agency has responded to part, or all, of the request is not intended, and shall not be construed to be a waiver by the Agency of all or any part of any objection to any request.\par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabTo the extent that any or all requests call for information that constitutes information or material prepared in anticipation of litigation, or for the hearing, or for information covered by the work product doctrine, or which constitutes information which is privileged by virtue of the attorney-client privilege, the Agency objects to each and every such request.  Accordingly, the Agency will not supply any information, materials or documents protected from discovery by virtue of the work product doctrine and/or attorney-client privilege.\par}{\pard\cf1\sl480\tabAlthough, as set forth herein, the Agency will make full disclosure of all discoverable documents as required by the applicable rules, the Agency asserts the following objections to Complainant\'27s discovery requests.  Each such objection is incorporated by reference in the response to each individual document request and section of each individual document request as though set forth fully therein.\line\par}{\pard\viewkind4\uc1\pard{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs24\sl480The Agency objects to each request to the extent it seeks information protected by attorney/client privilege or the attorney work product doctrine.\par{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}The Agency objects to each request to the extent that it seeks information that is neither relevant nor reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\par{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}The Agency objects to each request to the extent that it seeks employee personnel information (for employees other than Complainant) on the grounds that disclosure of such information will constitute an invasion of privacy of those employees as protected by the Privacy Act, 5 U.S.C. \'a7 552a (\'93Privacy Act\'94).\par{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}The Agency objects to each request to the extent that it is vague and ambiguous and to the extent that it does not describe the information or documents it seeks with reasonable particularity.\par{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}The Agency objects to these requests to the extent that they seek information or documents to which Complainant has equal access and which is in Complainant\'27s possession, custody, or control.\par{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\highlight7IF APPLICABLE:  The Agency objects to Complainant\'27s Interrogatories, Request for Admissions, and/or Request for Production of Documents as they exceed the number of Interrogatories allowed.  Agency responds to the Complainant\'27s first 30 interrogatories/requests, including subparts.\par\line\line}{\pard\cf1\b\qc III.  Specific Objections and Responses\b\par}\line{\pard\cf1\b\qc INTERROGATORIES\b\par}\line {\pard\cf1\ul INTERROGATORY NO. 1:\par}\line{\cf1\ul RESPONSE:}\line{\pard\line\cf1\highlight7The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it is overbroad and unduly burdensome.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it is overbroad with respect to time and scope.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it is vague and ambiguous, particularly with respect to the terms/phrases \'93_\'94 and \'93_____.\'94  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it is argumentative, requiring the adoption of an assumption of a fact that is not in evidence.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it seeks information that is irrelevant to the subject matter of this dispute and is not reasonably calculated to lead to discovery of admissible evidence.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds, and to the extent, that it seeks information protected from disclosure by the attorney-client privilege and/or attorney work product doctrine.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it seeks information protected from disclosure by the Privacy Act.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it is duplicative of Interrogatory Nos. _____, and thus, is unduly burdensome and harassing.  The Agency objects to this Interrogatory on the grounds that it contains discrete subparts, in contravention of the rules of civil procedure and the Acknowledgment and Order in this matter.\line\lineSubject to, and without waiving, the foregoing objections, to the extent that Complainant is seeking _______________, the Agency responds as 